# NobiTerminal fork fix (Wave 5 C1, 2026-11-26, v2): the NDK r30 flang toolchain's
# libflang_rt.runtime.a is built WITHOUT -fPIC, so its formatted-I/O objects
# (utf.cpp.o, unit.cpp.o, binary-to-decimal.cpp.o) cannot link into a shared
# library (ld.lld: "recompile with -fPIC"). arpack's formatted I/O is ONLY
# debug printing: 12 write(6,...) in the 6 *aupd.f drivers + 166 WRITE in the
# 9 UTIL print routines (cmout/cvout/dmout/dvout/ivout/smout/svout/zmout/zvout),
# which are compiled into libarpack and called from SRC when debugging. Removing
# all 178 WRITEs (+48 continuations) stops the linker pulling the non-PIC runtime
# objects in. Numerics untouched; the print routines become no-ops and the
# msglvl debug output goes away. The -fPIC Fortran flag alone cannot fix this:
# it only covers arpack's own objects, not the toolchain's runtime archive.
# (v1 removed only the 12 *aupd WRITEs; run 45859789229 failed identically on
# the same 3 archive members -- the UTIL WRITEs were the remaining source.)
